Phosphor Icons
--------------

cf:walkthrough diagram nodes inline icons from a curated subset of
@phosphor-icons/core 2.1.1, Copyright (c) 2023 Phosphor Icons, MIT License,
https://github.com/phosphor-icons/core. scripts/phosphor_vendor.rb builds
the subset from the pinned npm tarball into
scripts/vendor/phosphor/phosphor-2.1.1.json; the full license text is in
scripts/vendor/phosphor/LICENSE.txt. cf:prototype screens fetch the same
pinned package and write its notice into each walkthrough's
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, as diagram scenes with node icons do. cf:diagram
provider diagrams draw the same vendored glyphs as their fallback when a
provider icon is unavailable.

Cloud provider architecture icons
---------------------------------

cf:diagram provider architecture diagrams draw official cloud service
icons. No provider icon is stored in this repository. scripts/cloud_icons.rb
fetches each provider's icons at use time from a pinned npm package (named,
with its sha512, in skills/diagram/packs/<provider>.yml) into a local cache
outside git, and inlines the files unmodified into the diagrams a user
makes. The icons belong to the provider and are used under the provider's
own terms, which each diagram's notice comment and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
cite, not under the license of the package that carries them:

  AWS Architecture Icons, Copyright Amazon Web Services, Inc. or its
  affiliates. https://aws.amazon.com/architecture/icons/
  Fetched from @squinch/pack-aws (https://github.com/jquatier/squinch),
  which redistributes the icons unmodified.

The test suite uses only synthetic icons invented for it, under
test/fixtures/cloud_icons/fake-pack.
